## 5. Demo

*For each completed story, list the acceptance criteria and show that each one passed in the deployed build.*

*Presenter: be ready to explain and answer questions about every completed story, including work you didn't build.*

### Issue #3: *Player Health and Permadeath keep loop*

[Check] GGiven the player is currently in a dungeon run and has health remaining, When the player takes damage, Then the player's health decreases by the correct amount and the 8-bit health bar immediately updates to display the player's current health.

[Check] Given the player's health reaches 0 HP, When the final damage is received, Then player movement and actions are disabled, a death animation plays, and a "Game Over" screen is displayed after the animation finishes.

[Check] Given the player has died and the run has ended, When the player returns to the main menu, Then all unsaved run inventory and current-run gold are removed while any previously saved or permanent progress remains intact.

### Issue #5: *Enemy Defeated*

[Check] Given an enemy was alive, when that enemy's health reaches zero, then the enemy should "die"
[Check] Given an enemy is fighting the player, when the enemy "dies", it's appearance changes and it stops moving.

### Issue #60: *Enemy Creation*

[Check] Given the player enters a dungeon room, when they load in to the room, then there will be enemies that attempt to attack them
[Check] Given the player is in a dungeon room, when there are enemies in the room, then the enemies will approach the player
[Check] Given the player is in a dungeon room, when they are hit by an enemies attack, their health will decrease and may be given detrimental effects
[Check] Given the enemy is attacked by the player, when the enemies health reaches zero, then they will die, dropping loot and disappearing from the screen


### Issue #61 *Basic Spells* 
[Check] Given the player is in a dungeon room, when they press 1, then they will perform a melee attack
[Check] Given the player performs a melee attack, when an enemy is within range, then the enemy will lose health
[Check] Given the player is in a dungeon room, when they press 2, then they will perform a ranged attack
[Check] Given the player performs a ranged attack, when an enemy is hit by the ranged attack, then the enemy will lose health
[Check] Given the player is in a dungeon room, when they press 3, then they will create a blockade of some sort
[Check] Given the player creates a blockade, when an enemy runs into the blockage, then the enemy will recieve some kind of status effect related to the type of blockade.

